# QA Reporting

Apply when generating, editing, or interpreting test reports.

## Fresh run artifacts

Full test commands (`qa:all`, `test:all`, `qa:test`, and a default `qa` pipeline) delete **allowlisted current-run** artifacts (Playwright/Allure results, Postman/JMeter output, discovery JSON, Playwright result folders, temp logs) **before** the new run. Use `--keep-artifacts` to skip that clean. Manual: `npm run qa:clean` (`scripts/clean-test-data.ts`).

`qa:clean` must **never** delete the entire `reports/` directory, `reports/history/`, `reports/allure/history/`, or historical professional packs under `docs/input/qa-test-results/` or `docs/output/qa-test-results/` (including older timestamp folders and leftover flat files). Those are retained as evidence.

## Historical professional reports (retention)

- Each new `report:final` / Stage 19 run writes a **new** date-time folder `docs/input|output/qa-test-results/YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS/`.
- Never `rm -rf` the parent `qa-test-results` tree. Never overwrite an existing timestamp folder — if the same second is already taken, append `-2`, `-3`, …
- `docs/output/qa-test-results/latest.json` may be **updated** to point at the newest pack. That is not deletion of older folders.
- Documented in `qa.config.json` → `report.retention` and `docs/templates/qa-test-results.format.json`.

## Mandatory PKT execution archive (`reports/history/`)

Every `qa:all` / `report:final` execution also archives into a new folder:

`reports/history/<ProjectName>_<YYYY-MM-DD>_<HH-mm-ss>_PKT/`

- **PKT** = Pakistan Standard Time (`Asia/Karachi`, UTC+05:00). In this project PST means Pakistan — never US Pacific. Do not use the machine timezone.
- Project name sources (do not invent): `qa.config.json` `project.name`, then env `QA_PROJECT_NAME` / `QA_WEBSITE_NAME` / `QA_APPLICATION_NAME`, then a title already present in this run’s discovery, then the base-URL hostname (record that fallback in metadata).
- Never overwrite an existing execution folder. Collision: `_01` (or higher precision).
- Primary human report in that folder: `MASTER-QA-REPORT.html` (embedded findings in the release-readiness sequence — Executive Summary → Key Findings → scope/domains → Defects → Failure Analysis → Recommended Actions → Coverage Matrix → Release Quality Assessment, plus appendices — not a link-only index) plus `MASTER-QA-REPORT.json`. Generate via `scripts/reporting/generate-master-report.ts` after collect/coverage/final report and before/with the quality gate.
- Copy (do not move-only) existing module artifacts into `modules/` (discovery, accessibility, content, cross-browser, jmeter, performance, playwright, postman, responsive, security, seo, visual, workflows, failures, retest, coverage, quality, orchestrator, …). Copy this execution’s evidence into `evidence/` (screenshots, videos, traces, logs). Copy this execution’s Allure into `allure/` (results/report only — never `reports/allure/history`). Keep `execution-metadata.json` fields. Do not invent Allure or other suite reports that were NOT_EXECUTED.
- Top-level `reports/accessibility/` etc. remain temporary current-run write targets for engines (PATHS). `qa:clean` wipes those temp paths, never `reports/history/**`.
- `qa:clean` must never delete `reports/history/**` (including PKT folders, MASTER-QA-REPORT files, modules/, evidence/, and KPI JSON). Do not add `reports/history` to the cleanup allowlist.

## Professional reports

- **Master consolidated report** — `npm run report:master` (also from `qa:all` after archive) writes `MASTER-QA-REPORT.html` + `.json` into the PKT history folder from existing module JSON/MD. Missing modules stay NOT_EXECUTED / BLOCKED / N/A / UNTESTABLE.
- **Final unified report** — `npm run report:final` (and `qa:all` stage 19) writes `reports/summary/final-qa-report.md` + `.json`, then the five-layer professional SQA Word/HTML/PDF under a **new** date-time folder `docs/input|output/qa-test-results/YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS/`. Previous timestamp folders stay on disk. Stage 19 always runs at the end of `qa:all`, including after earlier FAIL stages and after `--fail-fast` stops. Tautological / observed-status API assertions are recorded as report-quality warnings and do **not** abort Word/HTML/PDF generation. MASTER-QA-REPORT is still written when the five-layer model fails quality checks.
- **Enterprise formats on demand** — `npm run docs:qa-report` regenerates DOCX/HTML/PDF from the same artifacts.
- **Raw tool artifacts** — stay in `reports/<tool>/`; index via `reports/summary/raw-index.md`, do not overwrite them.
- **Allure** — Playwright writes raw results to `reports/allure/results`. `npm run report:allure` (or `report:all`) runs `allure generate` into `reports/allure/report`. A previous `index.html` is copied to `reports/allure/history/<timestamp>/` before `--clean` so the only prior HTML is not wiped. Requires project deps `allure-playwright` + `allure-commandline` (Java JRE for the CLI). If the CLI cannot run, record **BLOCKED** — do not claim Allure works.
- **Playwright HTML** remains enabled (`list` / `html` / `json` reporters are not removed). `npm run report:playwright` prints suite HTML paths via PATHS.
- **Combined index** — `npm run report:all` generates/indexes Allure + Playwright HTML + existing Postman/JMeter + `report:final`, then writes `reports/summary/report-index.json`. Missing Postman/JMeter artifacts are **NOT_EXECUTED**; scores are never invented.

## Five report layers

1. Executive Summary  
2. Test Evidence  
3. QA Analysis  
4. Risks & Limitations  
5. Release Recommendation  

## Verdict rules

| Verdict | When |
| --- | --- |
| **PASS** | No P0/P1 application blockers; critical paths tested |
| **PASS WITH OBSERVATIONS** | P2/P3 issues or gaps documented |
| **FAIL** | P0/P1 application defects or critical path failures |
| **BLOCKED** | Required env, credentials, or target unavailable |

Never **PASS** while a P0 or P1 application blocker remains open.

## Evidence-based coverage

- Coverage in reports comes from **`npm run coverage`** and inventory artifacts — testable items with recorded outcomes ÷ total testable items.
- **Never fake coverage** — partial runs, skipped stages, and BLOCKED items must reduce stated coverage.
- **Never claim 100%** without `reports/coverage/coverage.json` and inventory evidence.
- List **uncovered functionality** in report sections and `docs/uncovered-test-items.md`.

## Defect classification

Use `npm run analyze:failures` before retest. Classes:

- **APPLICATION DEFECT** — wrong product behavior; do not weaken the test.
- **AUTOMATION DEFECT** — flaky locator, bad wait, wrong assertion — fix harness only.
- **ENVIRONMENT / CONFIG / TEST DATA / NETWORK / BROWSER** — fix env or document as BLOCKED.

## Integrity (non-negotiable)

- Never invent requirements / API endpoints / credentials / test results.
- Never hide failures.
- Never weaken assertions.
- Never claim complete coverage without evidence.
- **Never fake results** — only write statuses backed by execution artifacts.
- **Never weaken assertions** to achieve PASS.
- **Never omit failures** from summary or verdict.
- State the exhaustive-execution / no-silent-skip policy. List remaining BLOCKED / NOT_TESTED / REQUIRES_CONFIGURATION items with reasons.
- Severity: P0–P3 via `scripts/reporting/severity.ts`; broken links and auth failures are typically P1.

## Retest

After fixes, run **`npm run retest`** — preserves original FAIL records. Update final report only after retest evidence exists. Inspect existing report generators before changing them. After implementation, run `npm run report:final` (or the relevant report command) and fix actual errors. Do not merely say "looks good."
